  "pageVersion": "sha256:58c21d5fd8c2850cdee2cea028c4a94016c3cdb318de1effd97f9fe8c2482478",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_caa768187ce144baaee0c2bfc4b9da5d",
      "statement": "The design distinguishes two kinds of ambiguity: lookup-resolvable (answer exists in the world, fixable via context or tools) and judgment-required (answer is the user's own preference/priority), and the layer's purpose is to keep these from being conflated.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent-expertise-framework/01-narrow-interface/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L12-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8156c2adad0e168a60dc536c5e778afaead0c9d2a223c9bc5706b20afa3de943:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_91ebd97dddf44591959d8ad584cd8ef0",
      "statement": "The proposed pipeline extracts slots from the user utterance, checks conversation context/memory first, attempts a tool lookup if no value is present, and only generates a confirmation question after a lookup attempt fails/returns multiple candidates or if the slot was never lookup-eligible.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent-expertise-framework/01-narrow-interface/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L19-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7cec277d07d9448f71f98c58abb071471ea1388d2286e0ac440a6d94332cf1c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9e248b0d5bef4c4ebdaf8c3d6a86e50a",
      "statement": "Revisiting the incident shows the actual failure was not a wrong comparison between looking up and asking, but that the comparison/deliberation step itself never ran and an empty slot value went straight to question generation reflexively.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent-expertise-framework/01-narrow-interface/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L35-L35",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1fff8c38b2fca0c130f874f314243c5c739e295a3a3addec956cf2e42ff8bab7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_40dfa5b87371476d995966713678e10b",
      "statement": "Because the skipped step was the deliberation itself, the design concludes the layer must be a structural gate enforced outside the model's reasoning process (e.g., a question-asking tool call is only permitted if a lookup-attempt record already exists for that slot) rather than a checklist the model is expected to follow.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent-expertise-framework/01-narrow-interface/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L37-L39",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a933a50006285796d4767fa9507097461119be95df08db871d9a7d7e321c7a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b2c77eb5a09544c6944c658b7f69aafc",
      "statement": "Applying the pipeline retrospectively to the incident: the GitHub account slot was classified as lookup-resolvable via existing conversation memory, and a gh api call against 28 starred repos narrowed to exactly one match (langchain-ai/openwiki), which would have let the pipeline proceed without asking the user.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent-expertise-framework/01-narrow-interface/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L43-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d00535a0ce6fe6ac915712fe0c836963783741f48f07617d0522327cce7d6111:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d33abb693ab046c9887957c17ff26b8e",
      "statement": "Two open questions remain unanswered by the design: how to catch a lookup that resolves to a single wrong candidate, and how to generalize a rule for classifying whether a slot is lookup-resolvable rather than relying on post-hoc, incident-specific classification.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent-expertise-framework/01-narrow-interface/03-instruction-resolution-gate.md#L52-L53",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:885b65274ea2c9b34324a934560cfbfbc47c8a6737101b2f026dafb0211708f1:"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
